  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "When used",
   "texto": [
    "It is found in stories and biographies to present past facts as concluded: **nacque** (born), **fu** (was), **scrisse** (wrote).",
    "Their spoken use changes by region and style; it does not depend only on the fact being far away."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "More common forms",
   "texto": [
    "Regular verbs: **parlai, parlasti, parlò, parlammo, parlaste, parlarono**. Common irregulars: **fu / furono** (be), **ebbe / ebbero** (have), **fece / fecero** (do), **disse / dissero** (say).",
    "In a profession without determinant: **Nacque a Roma e fu medico** (born in Rome and was a doctor)."
   ]
